WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:02.578
Here is a grid, drawn as a picture.

00:00:02.578 --> 00:00:04.978
Nothing here is a forecast. The prices are

00:00:04.978 --> 00:00:07.512
illustrative. Watch the orders, then the buffer.

00:00:09.062 --> 00:00:11.929
Each candle shows four facts. The open, the

00:00:11.929 --> 00:00:13.984
high, the low, and the close. That is

00:00:13.984 --> 00:00:18.007
the whole candle. Buy orders sit below the

00:00:18.007 --> 00:00:20.175
price. Sell orders sit above it. When the

00:00:20.175 --> 00:00:22.598
price crosses a line, that order fills. A

00:00:22.598 --> 00:00:24.309
fill is not a promise. It is the

00:00:24.309 --> 00:00:26.657
price touching a level that was already placed.

00:00:28.207 --> 00:00:30.460
The shaded band is the range chosen before

00:00:30.460 --> 00:00:32.336
the start. The dashed line past it is

00:00:32.336 --> 00:00:34.976
liquidation. The gap between them is the buffer.

00:00:34.976 --> 00:00:37.261
When the buffer shrinks, the plan is under

00:00:37.261 --> 00:00:41.493
stress. Count the fills. Read the buffer. Keep

00:00:41.493 --> 00:00:43.371
those two numbers, and let the rest of

00:00:43.371 --> 00:00:44.037
the noise go.
